Subject: [PATCH] Physical-privacy SOFTWARE mic mute (zero captured PCM; no audio restart)
Target: prudynt-t @ f4b32289359d176fb0795d9f3735af0bd9d6d2fd (branch stable).
Stacks on: 0001-0006. Applies with git apply -p1 / patch -p1 AFTER them.

Mutes the microphone for physical privacy WITHOUT restarting the audio worker.
The earlier mic_enabled=false approach was reverted: it set global_restart_audio,
which on this build (USE_AUDIO_STREAM_REPLICATOR) tears down the audio worker under
the persistent RTSP audio replicator, starving it -> the go2rtc stream died (reboot
only). audio.mic_vol=-30 is live/no-restart but does NOT mute this T23 ACODEC.

This patch mutes in SOFTWARE: a runtime atomic `mic_muted` (NOT persisted, set live
via a new JsonAPI key with NO global_restart_*), and AudioWorker::process_frame zeros
the captured PCM into a reusable scratch buffer when set -- so the encoder, FIFO tap,
MP4 recorder, and RTSP/go2rtc feed all get true digital silence while frames KEEP
FLOWING (the replicator is never starved; nothing restarts; cannot wedge the encoder).

CRITICAL: process_frame operates on a LOCAL COPY of the frame descriptor. The IMP_AI
DMA frame handed to IMP_AI_ReleaseFrame must stay byte-identical to what GetFrame
returned -- IMP_AI_ReleaseFrame recovers the block's allocator header from
*(virAddr-20), so redirecting the RELEASED frame's virAddr would corrupt the free.
The copy is what gets pointed at the zeroed scratch; the DMA slot (data AND descriptor)
is never touched. Output/backchannel are NOT gated (privacy = don't transmit captured
audio). NUM_AUDIO_CHANNELS==1; muted is a relaxed atomic (single standalone flag).

Rootfs /sbin/physical-privacy drives it: do_on -> mic_muted true, do_off (verified-
lifted branch) -> mic_muted false, do_reenter -> mic_muted true. Boot/restart window:
the flag is runtime-only, so a fresh prudynt start is briefly audible until do_reenter
re-mutes (the originally-accepted boot window; no in-process privacy coupling added).

